commit 2524e12c8d1add11be5e1b721d5b9a0c02ae8517
Author: paulzierep <paulzierep@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 11:07:20 2026 +0000

    supervisor: wire auto-reporting into run_eval + fix flowchart, Zenodo record docs (issues #7/#8/#12/#15/#17)
    
    - run_eval.sh: after a successful eval, regenerate aggregate CSV
      (make_results_csv.py), per-bin CSV (make_per_bin_csv.py) and per-run
      bar chart + all-runs comparison scatter (make_per_bin_plots.py --all);
      generators best-effort so report failures never fail the eval.
      Deployed copy in /vol/data/benchmark/bin kept byte-identical; the two
      per-bin generators are now deployed there too.
    - make_results_csv.py: auto-derive dataset label and threads from
      run_meta.txt when not passed, so no-arg auto-runs produce complete rows.
    - make_per_bin_plots.py: new --all mode keeps the comparison scatter
      spanning every run with per-bin data, even when one run is re-evaluated.
    - README/docs/09: rewrite the optimization flowchart with renderer-safe
      mermaid syntax (no <br/>, no emoji in edge labels, explicit chains);
      gate rules now state big benchmark runs only after small+medium
      validation and parameter optimization on small sets first (issue #17).
    - docs/01/10/11: Zenodo record 22935025 metadata edited in place to MIT
      with an expanded description (no new version); DOI verified HTTP 200.

